  "materials": [],
  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Install app and configure sonar",
      "instruction": "Install the Fisher Deep app on a smartphone, launch it, and use it to establish a Wi‑Fi link (up to 80 m, extendable to 150 m) with the Deeper Chirp+2; customize beam angle as needed and set the acquisition mode to either “Bait Boat” or “Bank”, which enable the built‑in GNSS for positioning.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Prepare phone and initialize sonar",
      "instruction": "Put the phone in airplane mode to avoid Wi‑Fi interruptions, place the sonar in the water, and keep it submerged until the green GNSS indicator appears (≈1 minute) to ensure a stable GNSS lock; the sonar will automatically start recording once the water depth reaches at least 15 cm and data will be displayed on the app.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 2,
      "title": "Select acquisition mode and conduct survey",
      "instruction": "Choose the desired output mode and follow the corresponding field procedure:",
      "substeps": [
        {
          "instruction": "Bathymetry‑map mode – move the sonar continuously so that its path homogeneously covers the whole target area.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Cross‑section mode – follow a single transect; if multiple transects are required, keep the sonar out of the water for at least one minute between each transect to allow the algorithm to separate them, then re‑stabilize the GNSS lock before the next pass. The same transect may be repeated without interruption to improve accuracy. Record the distance from each river bank to the first and last sonar measurement (minimum depth 15 cm).",
          "title": ""
        }
      ],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 3,
      "title": "Optional: integrate external GNSS receiver",
      "instruction": "If higher positioning accuracy is needed, connect an external GNSS receiver/antenna (e.g., Android device running Open GEA or GNSS Logger) to record raw GNSS data, later process to RINEX and optionally apply PPK correction; after the survey produce a CSV file containing latitude, longitude and UNIX timestamp columns for the external GNSS points.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 4,
      "title": "Verify data storage and file handling",
      "instruction": "During acquisition the app saves data locally and uploads them to the free cloud account (https://maps.fishdeeper.com); the resulting file *bathymetry.csv* contains columns latitude (°), longitude (°), depth (m), temperature (°C) and time (Unix). Latitude/longitude are logged at 1 Hz under optimal satellite coverage, while depth and temperature are logged at 15 Hz. If all recordings span less than 24 h (even from different locations) they are automatically merged into a single CSV file.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
